      "title": "Saudi Arabia urged to reconcile with UAE to drive back Houthi separatists in Yemen",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/saudi-arabia-urged-to-reconcile-with-uae-to-drive-back-houthi-separatists-in-yemen",
      "description": "<p>Relations between the two countries soured in January when a UAE-backed force was defeated by Saudi Arabia in Yemen</p><p>Saudi Arabia is being urged to reconcile with the United Arab Emirates over Yemen as the price Riyadh must pay to form a military alliance capable of driving the Houthis back.</p><p>Relations between the UAE and Saudi Arabia in Yemen, where both had backed anti-Houthi forces, plummeted in January this year when a force with which it had been aligned – the separatist Southern Transitional Council (STC) – was attacked and defeated by Saudi Arabia in a move intended to squash its attempt to recreate a separate southern state. The UAE subsequently effectively quit Yemen.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/29/saudi-arabia-urged-to-reconcile-with-uae-to-drive-back-houthi-separatists-in-yemen\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-29T16:52:37"
    },
